/*
 * Zephyr's rpi_5 takes zephyr,sram from the SoC's sram0
 * (dts/arm64/broadcom/bcm2712.dtsi: 512 KiB at 0x200000, two address cells).
 * A GPU image carries a carve-out as statics, so sram0 is sized here, the way
 * the Pi 4 images do (driver/samples/zephyr/gl_test/boards/rpi_4b.overlay).
 * 32 MiB from 0x200000: the size the Pi 4's first runs used; pre-study-rpi5.md
 * (U10) says to keep it low until measured. Nothing in this overlay was run.
 * The same file sizes Zephyr's own hello_world in the gate row
 * (-DEXTRA_DTC_OVERLAY_FILE).
 */
&sram0 {
	reg = <0x0 0x200000 0x2000000>;
};
